{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Conduct a review with guidance for exits at attractions to skip gift shops",
        "additional_details": "Many families enjoy a day out at visitor attractions yet are often forced through gift shops on the only exit route. This can pressure parents \u2013 especially those on low incomes or with neurodivergent children \u2013 when kids ask for things they cannot afford and become upset; it spoils the end of a lovely day. We believe families deserve a choice \u2013 this is NOT about banning gift shops, just asking for an alternative exit where feasible, helping those with sensory overload or who need to leave quickly.",
        "background": "We want the UK Government to commission a review and publish national best practice guidance, encouraging visitor attractions \u2013 where physically feasible \u2013 to provide an alternative exit route so families don\u2019t have to go through gift shops to leave.",
